"Mark Horn" <hornm@enter.net> writes:
> I believe its an "M" but its definitely a 90.  We are trying to hook up our
> telephone switch to the decserver so we can telnet to the admin program on
> the switch.  The switch normally connects to a standard terminal with an RS
> 232 -DB 25 (male) connection.   The DECserver has an RJ45 connection.  Can
> anyone give me some advice on pinouts into the decserver, I have the
> standard pinouts from the telephone switch, but the DECserver is used and
> has no manual.

Get a BN25G-03 cable and a H8585-AB adapter for the serial port.
This will map it to a male 25 pin RS-232 connector.

You will then need a female/female null modem 25 pin RS232 cable to
interconnect the two devices.

I would suggest getting some of the docs, the DECserver 90M is a
rather foreboding black box without it.



