: line of drives I get hot swap and have even been able to add drives without
: rebooting the system!

Points of interest;
- DEC is still selling empty storageworks carriers (bricks).  I checked
myself.  Check the electronic store or call DECdirect.
- Heat is a pizzabox problem, not a drive problem, as all 4gig drives
run pretty hot (including barracudas).  At the time the pizzabox was
introduced, DEC 4gig drives didn't exist.  Another product, the BA350
cabinet, was fixed with an upgrade package, so I expect DEC simply 
couldn't engineer one for the pizzabox.
- Storageworks provides all the hot-swap advantages of Artecon.

I don't think there is enough here to sway a decision.  Local considerations
such as tolerance for Non-DEC equipment, sensitivity to price, and the 
discounts offered by DEC channel partners could sway this one way or the
other.

Glenn Hollinger,
University of Saskatchewan.



