Alpha is the fastest, and it offers better scalability due its true
64-bit architecture.  As for cost effectiveness.  That depends on a
couple of things.

	1.) Do you already have an upgradable Intel PC?
	2.) Do you mind spending more money upfront for the Alpha?
	3.) Is the application you want to run optimized for the 
	    Alpha?

The Intel platform is better *now* because it's cheaper, and just about
everything runs on i86 WNT.  Alpha is better because it provides better
long-term returns, since it's already 64-bit; and since it's faster,
you're faster.  Until the DEC deal with Samsung on ALPHA chip "OEMing,"
hopefully drops prices, I'd base my decision on the availability of the
application on Alpha.


						--Ed----->
