[Ed Webster]

> I have inherited an old microvax II running vms 5.4 does any one
> know if it is possible to network this to a TCP IP network ?. it has
> an ethernet board.

There are at least three options.  Digital, Wollongong and TGV all
sell TCP/IP implementations for VAX/VMS systems.  I've used them all,
and would not hesitate for a moment to recommend TGV Multinet.

On the other hand, and just in case you didn't know, you can run an up
to date UNIX on that machine if you want to.  NetBSD is a Berkeley 4.4
variant that runs on the VAX and on lots of other architectures, and
it's free.  Check out http://www.netbsd.org/ for more information.

-tih



