Assuming that he has the same cable that I do, (17-02358-01) the cable
is not a flat cable.  It is actually a round cable consisting of
individual wires at the connectors.  Adding another connector to it is
not practical.

Unlike the VAXstation 3100 cable, however, this cable ends (at the
controller) in a standard 50 pin header.  It would be possible to wire
up an extension ribbon cable to add additional connectors.  This cable
would go between the existing cable and the controller.

You would need a 50 wire flat cable, a 50 pin IDC header for one end, a
50 pin IDC socket for the other end, and a 50 pin IDC headers for the
middle for each drive you wish to add.

Good luck!

