If your Dec 3100 is as old as the one I've just got, and any of the
cable wires look the least bit brittle, I'd simply order a 5 connector
SCSI ribbon cable (or make it :) and replace the DEC cable completely.
You'll avoid the problems with keeping a bus (since the above scheme only
works correctly if you plug the extender into the original connector
closest to the end of the cable).  I don't know if the back SCSI connector
can take a ribbon connector, but the controller can take the regular
connector (considering that's what is there now).

Of course, the case doesn't really have space for three drives, and
I'd be careful that the power supply doesn't brown out under the extra
load.

Let us know how it goes.

David




