Steve Lionel wrote:
> switches to set.  The Truo 64 is actually a pretty good chip, but
> there are better nowadays.
> 

  The Trio64 is just a warmed over 864/964, and in turn is just a
  warmed over ISA bus design.  Having worked on a X server for this
  chip, I'm constantly amazed that it works as well as it does
  (and it does give pretty good performance) given the fact that the
  only thing in PCI I/O space is the frame buffer, and you can't even
  access that at the same time as you access the memory mapped I/O
  addresses (which are, of course, in ISA memory space).

  I'm guessing that the next generation from S3 will fix all this,
  and allow the programmers of the graphics code to sleep better
  at night ;-)

  The ATI Mach64 is a much nicer design (from a programmers
  perspective), but results in performance that isn't much better
  than the S3.



