I'm currently typing on a Sun-3/80 with one 110+ mb hard drive getting
a helping hand via an NFS mount from a nearby VaxStaion 3100 running VMS
and serving NFS through Multinet.  [Don't ask why, it just happened!  :-)]

The VAX is running Open-VMS 6.1 with 110+ and 500+ mb internal hard drives.
I have another 500+ mb HD for the 3100, brand new in the box.
The Sun is running SunOS. The Sun has 12mb RAM and the VAX, 16mb.
The Sun Monitor is a 17" color (slightly faded), 3100 has 20" B/W, sharp.

Unfortunately, the HD in the sun is dying.  I would like to simplify
this setup and maybe lower our elctric bill in the process!

Should I:

   1. Install the two 500 mb disks from the 3100 into the Sun-3 and
      retire the VAX?  (The disks are sccsi and I'm told this works.)
      (Do you know this to be true?)

   2. Install the second 500mb disk into the 3100, install Ultrix and
      retire the Sun?  (I want unix as my primary OS.)

   3. Install one of the 500mb disks into the Sun and maintain both
      machines as I have been.  (I don't like this for several resons.)

The resulting machine(s) will be a backup/alternative development and
prototyping web server as well as providing an X server for me.

I've been told that Ultrix is a dog on a VAX-3100. I've never benchmarked
any of these machines but my X-Server running under FreeBSD on a Gateway
2000/66mz seems peppier to me than X under Sun-OS on my Sun-3. :-)

I want to run the Apache web server on the resulting configuration.  It
runs well on my FreeBSD Gateway and I am told it will install on the Sun-3.
I don't know if Ultrix will accept it.

Thanks for your insights,

--Jim Fox



