Hi.

I spent the weekend assemblying an external SCSI HD and a CD-ROM and when 
I was ready to attempt installing Redhat Linux for the Alpha, I decided 
to upgrade the firmware on the machine since it arrived a mere couple of 
days ago with 3.5 (or something such) firmware..

The firmware upgraded OK, judging from the fact that the firmware version 
number is now different (I downloaded everything from ftp.digital.com as 
announced on a post to axp-list).  The downloaded files and instructions 
claim the firmware is version 3.8, but after the upgrade the firmware 
prints out version 4.33 or something such.  What went on didn't match 
what the readme.txt stated should read (for example, when my machine 
boots, it doesn't show SRM console then ARC console.. it just goes 
straight into ARC mode.) I also know it's upgraded because it now asks 
for a language, which it didn't ask for before.  In any case, both before 
and after the upgrade, the machine hangs at bootup when I do Switch to 
Digital Unix console (before the upgrade it used to say ... to OSF/1...)
The machine would just boot, flash the keyboard (I received no manual, no 
idea what each series of flashes mean but I remember seeing on some 
website that they mean something..) and nothing would happen.  I first 
solved this problem by disconnecting the internal battery for a few 
seconds and then simply having the machine come up and it'd tell me that 
something was inconsistent.. and I'd fix the time, etc. and it would be 
in NT console mode by default.. but I still wondered why it'd do that 
(ok, so since I don't have Digital Unix I'm not even supossed to select 
that...) and last time this happened, the machine hasn't come back to a 
full boot.  I tried changing the internal jumper from PUP (called PWR in 
the readme.txt of the firmware and failsafe loaded) to FSL and have the 
machine boot off the Failsafe disk.. nothing was output in either 
ocassion but in the previous ocassion this got me out of trouble when I 
set the switch back to PUP.. not this time.

Can anyone throw a magic bullet at me?  I really need to get this going 
today because I'm taking the machine out of the country and I'd like to 
have Redhat Alpha installed before I leave.. just to know that everything 
works, otherwise I'd have to leave the machine for servicing or 
something.. (how does servicing work, having bought the machine from a 
DEC OEM, can I get it serviced at DEC authorized service centers? free? 
the machine was bought only about 4 days ago)..

Please help! 

