references: <4uisum$6u2@dfw-ixnews6.ix.netcom.com> <4us41a$i4u@rs18.hrz.th-darmstadt.de> <1996Aug15.125635.16238@smiffy>
organization: Columbia University Department of Computer Science
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec.micro,comp.sys.dec


>>>In article <4uisum$6u2@dfw-ixnews6.ix.netcom.com>, ddb@ix.netcom.com (David Brockman) writes:
>>>> I have a basic VAXStation 3100, 3.5" floppy drive and 80 meg internal hard 
>>>> drive.  I have been using it with a serial terminal, but want to use the VR290 
>>>> color monitor and attach a bigger SCSI hard drive.  My questions are thus:
>>>> 
>>>> 1.  Where can I find the pin-out of the video connector?  I have looked at 
>>>>     severl 3100 specific FAQs and it does not appear to be in there.


RGB VAXstation 3100 umbilical cables use the following db15 pins:
D-Shell -- common ground
1       -- red core
2       -- common ground
4       -- mouse pin 1 (central block down, 1 == lower lefthand)
5       -- mouse pin 5
6       -- keyboard pin 2 -- common ground
7       -- common ground
8       -- keyboard pin 3 -- mouse pin 2 (counter clockwise from 1)
10      -- green core
11      -- blue core
14      -- keyboard pin 4 
13      -- mouse pin 7
15      -- keyboard pin 1 
ground  -- mouse pin 6

Mono VAXstation 3100 umbilical cables use the following db15 pins:
3       -- BNC Shell
9       -- BNC Core

plus the keyboard and mouse pins noted above. 

DECstation 2100s use the same mono video pinout, but cannot use
keyboard and mouse thru the umbilical cable. 







