Yes, each of the processors has a 64 bit pathway, with a 128 bit cache
pathway.the sun is 16 bits, sgi only
8 bits. The trick is throughput, the Digital Alpha systems have T-3
backbones, Fast-Wide SCSI-3 interfaces,
and a wide choice of lan and comm cards to choose.

The 8400 is the biggest bang for the buck. Proof? just log-on to the
internet and check out the download speed
of web pages. With a simple 14,400 modem in dial-up mode, 12 K bytes a
second is very common if the server is
a Digital Alpha. Most Sun servers best is 1.2 K bytes a seconds or less,
and ushally give messages like " 72
bytes ( stalled ) " . Just check it out for yourself.
Also Sun systems are overloaded with 64 modems, while 512 modems on a
Digital won't slow it down at all.

BOB.



