Although the base Windows NT operating system does not provide the ability to
run Intel Win32 binaries on a RISC CPU, it is my understanding that the FX!32
translator will provide this ability for Alpha Windows NT.

Intel Win16 binaries are handled by the Windows on Windows subsystem which is
present on all NT platforms (Intel, Alpha, PowerPC, MIPS).

I believe that FX!32 will be released around the same time as Windows NT 4.0,
and that it will be free.

