SGI has published a roadmap showing at least one more Alpha upgrade
for the T3 series.  Eventually, all SGI product lines will converge
on the MIPS chips.  Presumably, Cray/SGI will provide whatever
Alpha-MIPS conversion tools are appropriate.  Remember that the T3
was designed from the ground up to be a processor-independent
architecture.

Comparing microprocessors is a futile exercize.  Just a few months
ago, everyone was saying that only Intel and PowerPC would survive
and that SPARC would be the first to die, followed closely by Alpha
and MIPS.  Now PowerPC is sucking hind---- from a performance
perspective, and Sun is making money faster than it can count it. 
MIPS will be in a bazillion Nintendos, network computers and God
knows what else volume platforms.  Alpha continues to line up new
devotees, besides breaking virtually every performance recoird to
be had. PA-RISC is holding its own. Personally I think they will all
be around for at least another decade. 

