>There is only one test that is required and that is test T00.  This test 
>runs T22 if spun up or T23 if spun down.  Both tests are 'Total drive 
>sequence test'.  There is no built in formatter.  If your drive is 
>connected to an HSC the run 1, DKRFCT,  2, FORMAT.  You can also run DEC 
>diagnostics, and a licence to run them of course.

Then again, 99% of the times that people feel a need to format an RA
drive, they're just wasting their time.  Unless the drive has been
used in 18-bit mode, or unless some electronic problem has caused all
the blocks to be revectored (thereby overflowing the revector table),
there is no need to format the drive.  The term used "low level
format" is something that is exclusive to the PC world, where
formatting may be necessary to rid one's self of a virus.

Using test 00 will fully test the drive.  Run it once with the drive
spun down, spin it up and run it again.  If it passes, then you're all
set to start putting data on the drive.






