From: fdc@watsun.cc.columbia.edu (Frank da Cruz)
Subject: C-Kermit 6.0 Beta - VMS feedback/help needed
Date: 1996/08/17
Message-ID: <4v5a0c$5u6@apakabar.cc.columbia.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 174782598
organization: Columbia University
newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec



Hello, VMS folks.  I'm the author of C-Kermit, which many of you use.  I'm
finishing up version 6.0, but have not had much feedback or help from VMS
users, so "speak now or forever hold your peace".

Right now I'm getting together what I hope will be the final Beta edit.
There are still some holes in the VMS version that I, as not much more than
a VMS bystander, am competent to deal with.  So if any of you cares about
any of these things, now would be a good time to come forth and help out.

 . REDIRECT doesn't work.  If it did, we could add external protocol support
   for X-, Y-, and ZMODEM, assuming that XYZMODEM programs are available for
   VMS that allow their standard input and output to be redirected.

 . OPEN !WRITE does not work -- i.e. you can't open a process and write to
   its standard input.  (We do this with popen() in UNIX -- there's no popen()
   for VMS, at least not prior to version 7-point-something(?))

 . APPEND operations don't work quite right, and might leave behind holes in
   files.

 . There is evidently some secret for getting good file transfer rates over
   incoming LAT connections, because (as somebody claimed here recently) WRQ
   software can do it.  If anybody knows what the secret is, I'd like to
   know it too so we can handle LAT connections better.

 . Much that is unknown about making outbound LAT connections (e.g. from a
   modem on a LAT server)...  For documentation's sake: how to configure the
   LAT server and VMS for this, things to watch out for, etc.  And why does
   HANGUP not work on an LTAxxx connection?  What about LAT "groups" (whatever
   they are)???

 . There's no support for making DECnet or X.25 (VAX/PSI) connections (adding
   either of these would be a very big deal, and probably could not be done in
   time for version 6.0 anyway, but I thought I'd mention it).

 . The makefile is a mess: Alpha vs VAX; DEC C vs VAX C vs GCC; ...  Needs
   lots of cleaning up.  (This is of interest only to developers.)

If you have any other complaints about VMS C-Kermit, express them now --
preferably accompanied by helpful suggestions or offers of help.

Thanks!

- Frank



