X-Deja-AN: 173969122
references: <32100A28.98A@lincoln.ac.nz>
organization: University of Pennsylvania
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


In article <32100A28.98A@lincoln.ac.nz>,
Grant English  <english@lincoln.ac.nz> wrote:
| The Unix startup correctly identies the ethernet card DECChip 21040 or 
| something similar but then proceeds to configure the network on the 
| 10Base5 (or AUI) port.
| 
| Where should I look to change the configuration of said ethernet card?

In the SRM console, use the "show" command and grep for "ew":

P0>>>show | grep ew

This will show you all of the ethernet adapter related variables, the
one your looking for looks something like "ewa0_mode".  If you do a
"set ewa0_mode" (Or whatever that specific variable turns out to be),
it will complain and then list all of the different settings that you
can use to set the variable.  At that point, Digital Unix will
recognize the specified mode.

Roman




