In article <4uoqsi$vuv@csugrad.cs.vt.edu>, nurban@csugrad.cs.vt.edu (Nathan Urban) writes:

>I am considering acquiring a used PMAD-A TurboChannel Ethernet card.
>It's currently being used in a DECstation 5000/133.  I have a Personal
>DECstation 5000/25, running Ultrix 4.4.  Will it work in my machine?

The SPD for V4.4 indicates that up to 2 PMADs are supported on the
Personal DECstation.  I'd guess the limit of two corresponds to the
number of free TURBOchannel slots.

>If so, what is involved in installing it and getting Ultrix to
>recognize both it and the internal base card?

Install and verify that the console can see it.  In the kernel
configuration file, replicate the line for ln0 making it ln1.
The custom configuration file prefers to write all the lines
for devices with their actual location, and you can generalize
it using:

device          ln1     at ibus?        vector lnintr

I got this line from the GENERIC configuration file.  Rebuild
and boot using the new kernel.  You may want to do this before
installing the new adapter.

>I don't have any
>experience with making any external additions to my machine, and my
>support contract with DEC has long since lapsed..

The 2nd adapter needs to be on a different subnet.  With suitable
addresses, updating /etc/rc.local to add a new ifconfig line should
be pretty easy.  You might want to make the Personal DECstation a
router between the two subnets, but check with your local network
management group.

