The AlphaStation 255 workstations lately have come installed with SIMMs
labelled as 2x33 72 pin.  The memory that came with the AlphaStation 200
workstations works fine in the 255s.  The reverse it not true, the
AlphaStation 200s only see half the memory when these 2x33 SIMMs are
installed.  In other words, if we add 4 of these 8Mb SIMMs, only 4x4 or
16Mb shows up.

It appears that the new SIMMs only implement a single parity bit, while
the older SIMMs are of the 2x36 true parity variety.  Is there any way
to make use of the SIMMs that are shipped in the AlphaStation 255s in
other workstations?  We were expecting/hoping to add more memory to the
255s, and since this often requires removing SIMMs (as there are only
two banks available) from the 255s, we don't want any memory to go to
waste.



