Sorry, but "winchester" is a general technology label refering to disk
drives with integrated head/disk assembly in (semi) sealed containers.

This is similar to "xerox" refering to photoconductive drum/toner
deposition printing.  Or "hydromatic" transmissions using hydrolics
instead of gears.




