In article <4urn2a$vt@sloth.swcp.com>, phdewi@swcp.com (Phillip Williams) writes:
>Here is a problem that I cannot really understand. I have tk50/70 tpaes that 
>give me the write protect error even thru they're not write protected. I 
>even tried the tapes in a different tape unit but still they give me the 
>error. Would running them thru a bulk eraser do the trick or should be 
>just be used as a shooting target???

I've found that sometimes the little slide thingy that selects write enable 
or lock gets a bit loose/sloppy. Particularly in drives that are mounted
vertically, gravity can cause the tape to write-lock during operations. A 
piece of tape over the slide will keep it in place.

Another possibility if you have a mix of 50s and 70s is that you have a TK50
in a TK70 drive, or maybe vis-versa. A TK70 can _read_ a TK50 tape, but not
write one.
