>Here is a problem that I cannot really understand. I have tk50/70 tpaes that 
>give me the write protect error even thru they're not write protected.

What kind of tape drive?  CompacTape II (TK70) tapes originally written
on a TK70 can only be written on a TK70.  I don't know if writing one
on a TK50 will give a write error, but that would be a reasonable thing
to do.  For that you case do need a bulk eraser.  The same applies if
trying to write CompacTape I and II on the later DLT drive (TZ85, TZ86,
etc).

If you're trying to write a CompacTape I cartridge on a TK50, then it
should work, unless somebody write it on a TK70 once.

>I even tried the tapes in a different tape unit but still they give me the 
>error. Would running them thru a bulk eraser do the trick or should be 
>just be used as a shooting target???

As a shooting target would be more satisfying, but a bulk eraser will
fix many cartridge format problems.

