	I saw it happen in a farily short time, and on a system where the
heads were not loaded most of the time.  It was not long after the erruption
of Mt. St. Helens, and the vendor claimed that it was caused by airborne
debris from the volcano.  (It was distribution floppies for a Microprocessor
Development System.)  Now, we were on the east coast, near Washington, D.C.,
and in a climate controled and well filtered environment, so I tend to doubt
their excuse. :-)

