In article <320F6E1A.3009@pacbell.net>, Shale <Shale@pacbell.net> writes:
> Whenever we lose power, or have to power off our 11/785 reboots to a
> point where it asks for the date/time. Is there a bios batter on board
> that is supposed to save such info? Our service provider says there is
> not one, but I'm almost positive that the 11/785 would fully reboot
> w/out any prompts..

  The 78x has one standard and one optional battery backup unit. The standard
one is the TOD (Time Of Day) backup and it uses one battery. The optional one
is the main memory backup and it uses 3 of the same battery.

  If you open the 78x's front doors, you'll see a 19" rack on the left which
has the LSI-11 front-end processor and the TOD backup unit. Make sure the
TOD unit's AC on/off switch is on.

  These batteries die if left discharged for more than about 6 months - they
just won't take a charge.

  If you need the battery part number, send me email and I'll look it up
when I'm at the office, or you could call DEC at 603-884-5000 and ask for
"Part Number Assistance" - ask them for the part number for the battery as
I've described it above. Or, your old batter *might* have a DEC part num-
ber on it.

