In article <3208C68C.3DA@fwva.saic.com>, Scott Stark <stark@fwva.saic.com> writes:

:  Is it possible to run NT server 3.51 on the Alphastation 600 5/266?
:  
:  I realize from a marketing perspective that the AS600 is considered
:  a workstation but many desktop PC's which have no business running
:  NT server are doing just that.  Microsoft doesn't seem to care what
:  platform runs server just as long as the product/license is purchased.
:  
:  The official word I have gotten so far from DEC is that the AS600 is
:  only supported running Win NT client and NOT server.

  The key questions are "Will Microsoft support this?" and "Has the
  vendor told microsoft this has been tested?".  This information is
  (should be) part of the Microsoft NT HCL tables, somewhere underneath
  the URL http://www.microsoft.com/...

  Based on my (limited) knowledge of NT, the same core is used for both
  NT Workstation and NT Server, and if NT Workstation operates correctly
  on a particular system, its rather likely -- assuming the necessary
  incremental increase in memory and storage needed by/for NT Server is
  available -- NT Server _should_ operate correctly on the same system.

  (The converse is not necessarily true -- some systems may/will require
  capabilities packaged and included only in NT Server.)

