> 2.  Is the external SCSI connector a 'standard' 68 pin SCSI II connector or do 
>     I need a 'special' cable to go to an external hard drive?

  It's a weird beast. It looks like a wide SCSI cable, but if you look care-
fully, it's the wrong gender. It's a special cable for the VS3100, and is
narrow async SCSI. The cable is a BC56H and comes in -03, -06, and -09 var-
iants (for 3, 6, and 9 feet, respectively). The other end has a normal "Cen-
tronics 50" connector on it.

