This seems like a good time to complain again about Digital's failure
to follow through on a promise made at the Spring 95 DECUS symposium.

At that meeting, a public announcement was made that Digital would be
making ALL patches available on {ftp,www}.service.digital.com, to ALL
customers, irrespective of whether or not they had a software service
contract.  This was supposed to be in place by July of that year.  It
may have happened for VMS and/or NT (I was told that the VMS patches,
at least, were there more or less on schedule, but I haven't actually
checked to confirm), but the Digital UNIX ones *still* aren't there,
more than a year after they were supposed to have been.

A few are there, mostly security-related.  But the bulk of them still
are squirreled away, available only to people with support contracts.

At the Canadian DECUS symposium (February of this year) there was a
"Digital Listens" session, and the following exchange took place:

| Q:  During the Spring US DECUS Symposium last year, it was
|     announced that Digital would be making some software
|     patches for its operating systems freely available by
|     FTP.  As far as I can tell, this has been done for all
