It's quite correct and proper that a server not be supplied with 
the latest dazzling 3D accelerated graphics system. However, the 
AlphaServer 1000 takes this principle to a ridiculous extreme.

The Compaq ProSignia sitting next to our AlphaServer 1000 also has 
built-in VGA, with performance suited to a server, ie not like you 
would like on your desk, but adequete for the odd sysman task. The 
AlphaServer 1000 video isn't even useable.



Incidentally, this caused us some amount of grief recently. We had a 
disk crash and had to restore from tapes using Networker. I 
displayed the NW client on the console, and (because the console is 
so small) displayed the NW administrator somewhere else. The client 
lists the files as they are restored in a scrolable listbox. I 
noticed that the window could not keep up with the files as they came 
off tape. It only restored a randomish 20% of the files!

I did exactly the same again but this time I displayed both the 
client and the administrator else (on a PC running eXcursion). The 
client window kept up with the file restore rate and all the files 
were restored without a problem.

Seems like a combination of a bug in Networker and the slow 
AlphaServer 1000 console.


regards,
