In article <4uarmp$q65@bashir.peak.org>, masked@PEAK.ORG (Nick) writes:
:First of all, are consoles for these things [VAXstation II systems]
:available?
:I've been using the serial console port (after having removed the graphics
:controller cards), but I't be nice to have a graphical console to use with
:them..

   As you have pulled a graphical controller out of the system, you are
   apparently asking not for a controller, but for a display monitor. 
   In this vintage, some of the more common monitors were the VR260 and
   the VR290 series.

   The QDSS (called "GPX" or "Dragon") controller (M7169 and one or
   more M7168 modules -- visible on the end of the controller module)
   and the older QVSS graphics controller (M7602) video output are both
   RGB synch-on-green 1024 x 864 x 60Hz.  These and compatible monitors
   are certainly available `used'.  You'll obviously also need a video
   cable, an old-style mouse, and an LK201 or LK401 series keyboard.

:My other question is, what commands are available from the `>>>' prompt?

   Some of the more commonly used console commands are:

	   BOOT
	   BOOT ddcu
	   BOOT/R5:nnnnnnnn ddcu
	   TEST nn
	   INIT
	   UNJAM
	   DEPOSIT
	   EXAMINE

