robo@rumpelkammer.uni-mannheim.de (Robert Braeutigam) writes:


>Hello everyone,

>I recently got an old VAXStation 2000 for free. Unfortunately this box has
>no keyboard, no Display, no manuals, no anything.

>Does anyone know if and how I can connect a serial terminal to this box ?
>Or does anyone have the pinout for the display/keyboard plug ?
>Or do I have to use this thing as a doorstop ? Maybe a good idea...

>Thanks in advance...
>    
>	Robert

I used to have one of these.  The display/keyboard/mouse cable looks the
same as that from a VS3100, so that may be somewhere to look.  

The 9 pin serial (printer) port is the alternate console port.  It is wired
the same as any other 9 pin serial port, except that booting with pins 8&9
jumpered boots into alternate console mode.  So just make up a terminal cable
for this port with pins 8&9 shorted together.

Bruce




