We have used the VAXcluster Console Software (VCS) for a number of years 
to manage both DEC and non DEC systems. We were recently forced to 
upgrade from VCS 1.4 to POLYCENTER Console Manager (PCM) 1.6 because we 
required the ability to manage remote systems via TCP/IP.

We control our systems both from the C3 display using VXT 2000 terminals 
and via PCs using character cell terminal emulations (mainly Kermit 
3.14). Since upgrading we have found problems with the CONNECT function 
from both the C3 display and terminal emulators. Upon connect a number of 
screens of data are output (did not occur with VCS) but the display is 
cleared after each screen. Looks good at 300b but not much use at 9600b 
and above. This completely screws up the Kermit display  Also it does not 
display correctly on VXT 2000 DECterm sessions (lots of backwards ? 
marks). This could be something to do with the large number of DCS 
characters output by PCM (without parameters) but we are not sure.

The EXTRACT/REVIEW function is less than optimal from the C3 display when 
using DECterm sessions from a VXT. The data is output and the display 
scrolls up but the session is immediately terminated once output is 
complete. Not very useful. Previously under VCS the data was output a 
screen at a time.

Are we alone in having these problems or are there large numbers of you 
suffering in silence. If the latter, please log all problems with Digital 
Support to raise the profile of these problems.


