We ran into the exact same problem with a similar configuration last November. 
The answer from VMS support was "it will not work".  They said there is no 
patch for the problem.  If you search through DSN you can probably find a note 
on it.  Search for Seagate and 5.5 and that should get you close.  

As I remember the problem is limited to that Seagate (and possibly others 
in that line) and VMS 5.5-H4. DEC says that the Seagate returns "too much" 
information when VMS queries the drive. VMS does not understand what it 
is getting back from the drive and will not mount it.  

We we staging an upgrade and wanted to get a system disk backup upgraded to 
VMS 6.2 but did not have a disk big enough in the VS3100.  I went to a local 
computer store and bought the Seagate 1 gig Hawk and restored a backup of the 
5.5-H4 release to it.  It would not boot.  You cannot image our surprise 
when we found that it could not be made to work!  We ended up building a 
temporary system disk on a borrowed drive from the local DEC rep and upgraded 
it to 6.0.  Then we moved it to the Seagate and upgrade to 6.2 on the Seagate.

HTH,

gozer

