> PDP 11/04 connect terminal is RS232 20mA current loop.

EIA-232 and 20mA current loop are two completely different things.
To connect your 11/04 to EIA-232 you will need some sort of converter;
this sort of thing is available from Black Box:

	http://www.blackbox.com/bb/products/p34.html/tiga6f0

(I have no connection to Black Box.)

If you're cheap but handy with electronics you can build your own converter
with some optoisolators etc.; unfortunately I don't have any plans or
schematics.

Some DEC equipment can be strapped for either EIA-232 or current loop, but
I don't think the 11/04 console port can.  Perhaps someone with more 11/04
experience can confirm or refute this.

Cheers,
Eric



