>I have 2 questions:
>
>(2) How do I get 16Mbyte RAM? Is it possible mixing DEC and Clearpoint
>cards. 

The Clearpoint should work.

Here's how the Ba123 backplane works...
In the first 4 slots the cpu goes first then Memory. As you can see the shows 3
Memory boards, the backplane will handle the memory just the MVII won't. You can
place a Mv3600 here and use the extra slot for memory. But I digress... If one
doesn't fill all 4 slots one has to place a jumper card in the top part of the
backplane. (The M number escapes me...)

But you may place in the un-used slots other boards. I've placed in there Emulex
disk controllers or a Deqna comes to mind. The reason for this is that the
interrupts run straight thru slots 1-4 on slot 5 the interrupt comes into that
slot then goes down the slot into slot 6. Then in slot 6 it goes up an out to
slot 7 and so on...

As you can see this is quite different from a Ba23 where the interrupts run
serpentine all the way down the backplane. Any question just ask.


