In article <francini-0508960013030001@news.ultranet.com>, francini@ultranet.com (John J. Francini) writes:
>In article <ERIC.96Aug2160212@goonsquad.spies.com>,
>eric@goonsquad.spies.com (Eric Smith) wrote:
>
>> Is the TU81 a normal Massbus tape drive?
>
>No, not that I'm aware of.  It was a horizontal tape drive that connected
>to an HSC-xx, so it was a DSA device, like an RA81. It could also be used
>directly on VAXen if they had some sort of DSA disk/tape controller, like
>the KDA50, KDB50, etc.

You're thinking of the TA81.  The TU81 used a KLESI interface.  And, neither of
them could be connected to a MASSbus.

>Instead of one of those boat anchors, why not get a real drive, like a
>TU78?  Those came in a variant that would talk to a TM03 controller, I
>thought...

Actually, the TU78 used the TM78 controller.  The TM03 would only do NRZI and
PE modes, while the TM78 only did PE and GCR modes.  The TU78 never connected
to a TM03, though.

