The example I gave of a transparent (8") floppy actually occured 
overnight.  <shudder>

>Another consequence of this is that the drive motor runs.  and runs.  and
>runs...without ever stopping.  Not always a good idea...

Note of course that 8" floppy drive spindle motors are *much* bigger than
5.25" floppy drive spindle motors, presumably coz you need more torque to
spin an 8" floppy in its jacket.  That makes stopping and starting the
spindle rather less of an option than on the relatively tiny motors found
on 5.25" drives.  

