How many of you remember the drums on the old AN/FSQ-7 computer
used in the SAGE air defense system?   For the youngsters in the
crowd, this computer used 58,000 vacuum tubes and was in use
(defending our country from attack) until at least 1983 or 84.
The one I visited was at North Bay, Canada, underneath 700 feet
of solid granite.   The entrance to the site (including the 
giant vault doors) looked just like the one in the movie
"Wargames".

The heads were mounted in a threaded holder that allowed a
technician to adjust the head-to-disk gap.   The technician
explained the adjustment procedure: "You screw them down
carefully until you hear them touch, then back them off a bit".

For the terminally curious, this machine is now located at
The Computer Museum in Boston.

